Fixes the PHP 8.4 deprecation "Implicitly marking parameter $connection / $resource as nullable is
deprecated, the explicit nullable type must be used instead" raised by
Wyomind\GoogleProductRatings\Model\ResourceModel\Review\Collection::__construct().

Root cause: the constructor declares "Type $param = null" without "?", which PHP 8.4 deprecates.
Fix: declare both parameters explicitly nullable ("?Type $param = null"). No behaviour change.

diff --git a/Model/ResourceModel/Review/Collection.php b/Model/ResourceModel/Review/Collection.php
index 267f1e7..1fc20f5 100644
--- a/Model/ResourceModel/Review/Collection.php
+++ b/Model/ResourceModel/Review/Collection.php
@@ -19,8 +19,8 @@ class Collection extends \Magento\Review\Model\ResourceModel\Review\Collection
         \Magento\Review\Model\Rating\Option\VoteFactory $voteFactory,
         \Magento\Store\Model\StoreManagerInterface $storeManager,
         /** @delegation off */
-        \Magento\Framework\DB\Adapter\AdapterInterface $connection = null,
-        \Magento\Framework\Model\ResourceModel\Db\AbstractDb $resource = null
+        ?\Magento\Framework\DB\Adapter\AdapterInterface $connection = null,
+        ?\Magento\Framework\Model\ResourceModel\Db\AbstractDb $resource = null
     )
     {
         $wyomind->constructor($this, $wyomind, __CLASS__);
